gate.code_cataloged.unmet_exports:
%d symbol(s) exported by `%s` that the spec does not catalog: %s.

A symbol outside the catalog crosses the pipeline without a rule to confront — no one knows what it should do.

Two solutions: catalog it in the spec (the NAME just needs to appear in the text of a rule), or declare that it carries no rule — on the symbol's line, or in the comment directly above it:
    // @no-rule: <why this symbol has no rule>
    export function algo() { … }

gate.obligation_honored.fail_unfulfilled:
unfulfilled cross-cutting obligation: %s. Three ways out, and only one is silence:
  1. FULFILL the duty;
  2. if it will be paid later, assume debt with `obligation_pending: <name> — <when/where>` (remains Pending in report, visible);
  3. if duty DOES NOT apply to this node, waive with `obligation_waived: <name> — <reason>`.
Waiving what is still owed is dishonest; leaving red what has already been acknowledged confuses debt with neglect.
